(f) Providing education, prevention of impairment, posttreatment monitoring, and support of rehabilitated impaired license holders; and
(g) Performing other activities as agreed upon by the disciplinary [disciplining] authority.
(2) A contract entered into under subsection (1) of this section may be financed by a surcharge on each license issuance or renewal to be collected by the department of health from the license holders of the same regulated health profession. These moneys shall be placed in the health professions account to be used solely for the implementation of the program.
